<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rafael Antonio Gutiérrez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1845–1921</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rafael Antonio Gutiérrez was a Salvadoran general and Liberal president of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> from 1894 to 1898. He came to power through a revolt against Carlos Ezeta and joined Honduras and Nicaragua in the Greater Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>. In November 1898 he was overthrown by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-regalado">Tomás Regalado</a>, who withdrew El Salvador from the union, which then collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rafael-antonio-gutierrez.jpg" alt="Rafael Antonio Gutiérrez" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rafael_A._Gutierrez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
